{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/424219-elements-of-demon-and-non-iremite-arisen","id":424219,"title":"Elements of Demon, and non-Iremite Arisen","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-01T09:35:24-08:00","id":424219,"title":"Elements of Demon, and non-Iremite Arisen","content":"It's been strongly established that Irem is the One True Source of the risen, and any mummies from other places are their own, lesser things. That said, <b>Demon</b> deals with elements like time travel and alternate realities, which can result in settings drastically different from the baseline WoD. With this being the case, is it not conceivable that in some Other Place the Arisen were created by a proto-Incan, Chinese, or what-have-you culture, rather than proto-Egyptian Irem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T10:27:10-08:00","id":424288,"title":"","content":"If it would make a fun and compelling game for you, why not? I wrote much information on the Wu'tian and Teomallki back in the days of Mummy: The Resurrection and loved their distinctive takes on the mummy condition.<br /> <br /> That said, there are a few challenges in adapting Mummy: The Curse to other cultural contexts. These aren't unsurmountable, but need to be addressed. First up are Pillars, each of which correspond to Egyptian conceptions and divisions of the soul. You could create a different set of Pillars that reflected alternate cultural perspectives, but then you have to remap and redefine all the Decrees, plus convert the Soul Affinity and Utterance prerequisites to your new Pillars (or else start fresh and write a completely new set of powers which is a *monumental* task). Furthermore, the thematics of many mummy powers resonate with the imagery of occult empires, formalized guilds of art forms, desert power, animals sacred to Egyptians, and the mythological elements of ancient Egypt like the Judges and other gods. Accordingly, you'd need to decide the social splats for your new mummies since they wouldn't follow the guilds that the Arisen use.<br /> <br /> If you can do all this, you have my utmost respect. Just understand how big your task will be before you embark upon it.<br /> <br /> One way to sidestep many of these issues is to assume a diaspora of mummies from Irem. If mummies spend most of their arisings since the diaspora amidst other cultures with local cults that have their own mythologies, these Deathless will have many more memories of being South American or Chinese while still retaining the systems and soul divisions that are embedded in Mummy: The Curse. With lower Memory ratings, these mummies may not even realize they were created in another part of the world to the point that they would dismiss such allegations if confronted by Deathless who were more aware of their true past. Alternately, Deathless in diaspora may well remember their origins in Irem, yet have since distanced themselves from their past to immerse in other cultures that they have grown to prefer.<br /> <br /> Does all that make sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T14:12:30-08:00","id":424493,"title":"","content":"Hmmm. Well, as far as Pillars go, I'd need to know more about how the individual cultures viewed the soul. Since you authored much of the Teomallki and Wu'tian write-ups for Resurrection, do you have any advice on sources to start my search with?<br /> <br /> Alternately, I suppose I could pare the Pillars down to their core defining elements (Shadow, Heart, etc.) and just re-skin them with culture-appropriate names.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T16:26:19-08:00","id":424641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/424219-elements-of-demon-and-non-iremite-arisen?p=424493#post424493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm. Well, as far as Pillars go, I'd need to know more about how the individual cultures viewed the soul. Since you authored much of the Teomallki and Wu'tian write-ups for Resurrection, do you have any advice on sources to start my search with?<br /> <br /> Alternately, I suppose I could pare the Pillars down to their core defining elements (Shadow, Heart, etc.) and just re-skin them with culture-appropriate names.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I did that writing back in 2002. I'd probably have to track down my books to reconstruct the answers to that. I do recall there not being any sort of neat fivefold divisions among either type of mummy, though. If I can find time, I'll see what I can find, but your best bet may be to pick up a pdf of the Mummy: The Resurrection Players Guide if you can find it. (Fun fact: It was the first book I had an author credit on.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T16:56:19-08:00","id":424668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephilpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/424219-elements-of-demon-and-non-iremite-arisen?p=424288#post424288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One way to sidestep many of these issues is to assume a diaspora of mummies from Irem. If mummies spend most of their arisings since the diaspora amidst other cultures with local cults that have their own mythologies, these Deathless will have many more memories of being South American or Chinese while still retaining the systems and soul divisions that are embedded in Mummy: The Curse. With lower Memory ratings, these mummies may not even realize they were created in another part of the world to the point that they would dismiss such allegations if confronted by Deathless who were more aware of their true past. Alternately, Deathless in diaspora may well remember their origins in Irem, yet have since distanced themselves from their past to immerse in other cultures that they have grown to prefer.<br /> <br /> Does all that make sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought this the diaspora was part of the default setting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}